---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Layout title="Data Safety – KAOS" description="KAOS data safety summary: what the game collects, why, and how to delete it.">
  <section class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Data safety</p>
      <h1>Data safety.</h1>
      <p class="lede">A plain summary of the data KAOS handles, matching the Data safety section on Google Play.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <article class="container prose">
      <p><strong>Last updated: October 2026.</strong></p>

      <h2>Summary</h2>
      <p>KAOS has no account system and no ads or analytics. It only sends data when you choose to submit a score to the optional leaderboard. The game is fully playable offline.</p>

      <h2>Data collected</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Data type</th><th>What exactly</th><th>Collected</th><th>Shared</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th>Personal info → Name</th>
            <td>The nickname you type on the leaderboard (up to 20 characters)</td>
            <td><span class="pill pill-yes">Yes, optional</span></td>
            <td><span class="pill pill-no">No</span></td>
            <td>App functionality (rankings)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th>Personal info → User IDs</th>
            <td>A randomly generated installation identifier (not your Google or device advertising ID)</td>
            <td><span class="pill pill-yes">Yes, optional</span></td>
            <td><span class="pill pill-no">No</span></td>
            <td>App functionality (deduplicate leaderboard entries)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th>App activity → Other in-game actions</th>
            <td>Survival time / score</td>
            <td><span class="pill pill-yes">Yes, optional</span></td>
            <td><span class="pill pill-no">No</span></td>
            <td>App functionality (rankings)</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>“Optional” means nothing is sent unless you submit a score. The nickname and score are visible to other players on the leaderboard.</p>

      <h2>Data we do not collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No email address, password, phone number, or contact list.</li>
        <li>No precise or approximate location.</li>
        <li>No photos, videos, audio, files, or messages.</li>
        <li>No health, financial, or payment information.</li>
        <li>No web browsing history or app usage analytics.</li>
        <li>No device advertising ID and no cross-app tracking.</li>
        <li>Motion/accelerometer readings are processed on-device and never sent.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Sharing</h2>
      <p>We do not sell or share your data with third parties. Score data is sent only to the KAOS leaderboard server so it can display rankings. If you use the Android share sheet, the text goes only to the app you pick.</p>

      <h2>Security practices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Encrypted in transit:</strong> the official KAOS leaderboard server uses HTTPS.</li>
        <li><strong>No account data at rest:</strong> we do not hold emails, passwords, or payment data.</li>
        <li><strong>Deletion request:</strong> you can ask us to remove a leaderboard entry.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Ads and analytics</h2>
      <p>KAOS has no advertising, no analytics, and no third-party tracking SDKs. The only third-party code is the Godot game engine.</p>

      <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
      <p>Local scores and settings are deleted when you clear KAOS's app data or uninstall the game. To remove a leaderboard entry, email <a href="mailto:emavgl.app@gmail.com">emavgl.app@gmail.com</a> with the nickname and approximate score.</p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>KAOS is a general-audience game and is not designed for children under 13. Leaderboards are optional and use only a nickname.</p>

      <p class="small-note">See the full <a href={`${base}privacy-policy`}>Privacy Policy</a> for details and your rights.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</Layout>
